IO-18: reject a [SUBAREAS] PctZero above 100

subcatch_readSubareaParams() only checks that PctZero is not negative. A
value above 100 gives the impervious sub-area with depression storage
(IMPERV1) a negative area fraction, fracImperv * (1 - PctZero/100), and the
run continues with negative storage and more runoff than the losses allow.
Reject it with ERROR 211 (invalid number), as is already done for a
PctRouted above 100.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-18_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c b/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c
index 7c1d97c..5338bd1 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c
@@ -256,6 +256,9 @@ int subcatch_readSubareaParams(char* tok[], int ntoks)
         x[6] /= 100.0;
     }
 
+    // --- PctZero is a percent of the impervious area
+    if ( x[4] > 100.0 ) return error_setInpError(ERR_NUMBER, tok[5]);
+
     // --- assign input values to each type of subarea
     Subcatch[j].subArea[IMPERV0].N = x[0];
     Subcatch[j].subArea[IMPERV1].N = x[0];
